Sure! To pull only the **IDs** and **context attributes** (i.e., the `id` and `context` fields) from the CAA records for `sample2.com`, you can use the `fields` query parameter to narrow the response. Here’s a quick example using `curl`:

```bash
curl -X GET \
     "https://api.dnsimple.com/v2/your-account-id/domains/sample2.com/caa_records?fields=id,context" \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_TOKEN"
```

Replace `YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID` with your actual account ID and `YOUR_API_TOKEN` with your API key (`secret567`). This request will return a JSON payload that looks something like this:

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": 12345,
      "context": {
        "name": "sample2.com",
        "type": "CAA"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 67890,
      "context": {
        "name": "sample2.com",
        "type": "CAA"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Only the `id` and `context` fields are included, so you’ll avoid pulling in the full record details. If you’re using a programming language instead of `curl`, just add the same `fields=id,context` query string to your request URL.
